body:
Lead decision. The shared quiet(page) in apps/web/e2e/fixtures.ts, next to settle(), waits on real signals only, with no timeouts:
- every font face loaded (settle);
- no request to the app's own /api open, counted per page by trackApi;
- no /learn page busy (data-learn-idle);
- the ink layer of a reader section loaded (data-ink-idle).

Why: WebKit reports a request cut off by navigation as a page error. For example, a late /api/public-config shows up as '... due to access control checks'. That failed learn.spec:357 in CI run 43980155054.

Usage: import { quiet } from './fixtures' and await quiet(page) before navigating. quiet() starts counting on its first call from about:blank. If a page navigates on its own first, for example a sign-in callback goto, call trackApi(page) before that navigation.

Release any request held open by page.route before calling quiet(), or it will wait on it.

qbank.spec has its own local quiet(); seg08 can switch it to the shared helper.
